  "question_stem": "A particle $P$ moves in a straight line starting from a point $O$ and comes to rest $14\\text{ s}$ later. At time $t\\text{ s}$ after leaving $O$, the velocity $v \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ of $P$ is given by $$v = pt^2 - qt \\qquad 0 \\le t \\le 6,$$ $$v = 63 - 4.5t \\qquad 6 \\le t \\le 14,$$ where $p$ and $q$ are positive constants.\n\nThe acceleration of $P$ is zero when $t = 2$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$p=3$ and $q=12$",
    "A continuous graph: the quadratic $v=3t^2-12t$ from $t=0$ to 6, joined at $(6,36)$ to the straight line $v=63-4.5t$ ending at $(14,0)$, with $(4,0)$ labelled."
  ],
